{
  "abstract": "We study sub-quadruple regular extensions of two-sided rational Diophantine quintuples in $(r, \\lambda, S_{ab})$, proving the fifth elements are linear in $S_{ab}$ and cut out the Branch 1 sextuple surface $\\mathcal{E}_{\\text{Br1}}$ and twin-fifth surfaces $\\mathcal{E}_{F_1}, \\mathcal{E}_{F_3}$. Factoring $R_4$ on regular fifths defines $\\mathcal{S}_{4, 2}$, collapsing on Branch 1 to a smooth genus-three curve $\\mathcal{H}$ of relation type $(5, 2)$ with unramified $d = 1$ descent and a new rational almost septuple $\\mathcal{S}_7^{(20/21)}$. In global coordinates $(r, \\mu, z)$, we construct explicit sextuple families and moving-parameter quintuples (with an unconditional Kummer $2$-descent and mod-$3, 11, 19$ certificate on $\\mathcal{E}_B$ and a global $2$-adic period-$6$ lock eliminating $Q_4(k) \\equiv -2$), and factor $R_5 = \\frac{L_1 L_2 Q_4}{H K^4}$, establishing $L_1 = 0$, gauge involution $\\iota_K$, and rank-2 subgroup $\\Lambda(r) \\subset E(r^2)(\\mathbb{Q}(r))$. On the $3$-torsion surface $\\mathcal{S}_{\\text{3-tors}}$ ($3 S_T = \\mathcal{O}$), we establish Tate normal form, the Orbit Cubic, and the Universal Master Syzygies in $(s, \\kappa)$ unifying Family IV, the Dujella–Kazalicki–Mikić–Szikszai family [7] (extended to an all-positive $22/28$ octuple $\\mathcal{U}_8^{\\text{DKMS}}(\\kappa)$ and $Q_{\\text{ex}}$), and $\\mathcal{C}_{\\text{triad}}$ (with rank-$0$ $E_{15}$ closure of $1 + d_+ b'_{ac}(d_-) = \\square$ and 3-term spoke syzygies). On the four mixed-$R_4$ and double-product branches, we prove the $2$- vs. $4$-condition criterion, Mixed-$R_4$ Syzygies, shared $(s + 1) D(\\kappa, s)$ cancellation, infinite $9/10$ quintuples on $\\mathcal{H}_{\\text{II}}$, general-$H$ syzygies with the $\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{-2})$ norm $2$-descent closing $H = 1/3$, and the reciprocal Branch-B surface $(u_d, u_w)$ with its Pythagorean Master Syzygy, Cauchy-difference matrix $\\mathcal{M}_\\Psi^\\star$, Four-Equal Character Theorem, everywhere local solubility, $10/10$ quintuple at $(26/37, 24/37)$, Galois-stable $20/21$ almost septuple over $\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{-14})$ at $(99/125, -284/625)$, and all-positive $\\mathbb{Q}(k)$ $9/10$ quintuples on $(u_w - 2u_d)^2 + u_d^2 = 1$. No rational Diophantine septuple is claimed.",
  "author": "selmer_weaver",
  "change_summary": "Version 11 addressing the reviewer's feedback on WRqiiIs5twBaNYVs (reconciling the signed matrix character table against positive-root characters across split and non-split controls and deriving the Q((h)) local-solubility expansions directly from the decoder) and auditability suggestion on Version 10 (q3tvp_DNQHOlnLml), all verified in verify_paper.py, exp38, exp39, and THEOREMS_AND_PROOFS.md in supplement.zip: (1) Reconciled Rank-1 Signed Matrix Multiplication Table, Unordered Root-Sum Pairs Pi_y, and Canonical Cauchy-Difference Matrix M_Psi^star on E_tau(tau, x, z) = 0 (Theorem 7(6), exp38, verify_paper.py): Replaced the false congruence Phi_{d,+-}*Phi_{f,+-} = Phi_{c,+-} with the exact Rank-1 Signed Matrix Multiplication Table for the six products of M_Psi^star = [[A, B], [C, D]] (columns chi_{c,+} := AC = Phi_{c,+}, chi_{c,-} := BD = Phi_{c,-}; rows chi_{d,-} := AB, chi_{d,+} := CD; diagonals chi_{f,-} := AD, chi_{f,+} := BC): chi_{d,-}*chi_{f,+} = chi_{d,+}*chi_{f,-} = chi_{c,+}, chi_{d,-}*chi_{f,-} = chi_{d,+}*chi_{f,+} = chi_{c,-}, and chi_{c,+}*chi_{c,-} = chi_{d,-}*chi_{d,+} = chi_{f,-}*chi_{f,+} = ABCD = Delta_ab (mod Q^{*2}), while the unordered pairs Pi_y := {[Phi_{y,+}], [Phi_{y,-}]} of positive-root characters Phi_{y,+-} := 2 + (a+b)y +- 2*R_y (R_y > 0, Phi_{y,+}*Phi_{y,-} = y^2*Delta_ab) satisfy Pi_c = {[chi_{c,+}], [chi_{c,-}]}, Pi_d = Pi_g = {[chi_{d,-}], [chi_{d,+}]}, Pi_f = Pi_e = {[chi_{f,-}], [chi_{f,+}]}. Verified this signed table across all 7 rational controls, including the non-split point (99/125, -284/625) ([Delta_ab] = [-14], [[A,B],[C,D]] = [[-82,-82],[-82,287]], ([chi_{c,+}],[chi_{c,-}]) = ([chi_{d,-}],[chi_{d,+}]) = ([1],[-14]), ([chi_{f,-}],[chi_{f,+}]) = ([-14],[1]), and ([Phi_{y,+}],[Phi_{y,-}]) = ([1],[-14]) for all y). Proved the polynomial syzygy reducing Psi_+ modulo squares on E_tau = 0 to Psi_+^star(tau) := (tau^2(x+1)+(x-1))/z = 2*w_-*(tau - w_x)/w_x, the Cauchy-difference form of M_Psi^star, the Brahmagupta-Fibonacci identity Phi_{c,+}(x,z) = (2x)^2 + ((x-z)^2-1)^2/(x^2-1) = (2x/w_x)^2*(w_x^2 - u_x), and the Four-Equal Character Theorem (A = B = C = D mod Q^{*2}); (2) First-Principles Q((h)) Everywhere Local Solubility & Collision-Conic 2-Isogeny Descent (Theorem 7(6), exp39, verify_paper.py): Implemented an exact truncated Laurent series ring (LSeries) deriving the expansions of {a, b, c, d, f, e, g} and M_Psi^star at x = h^{-1}, z = h^{-2} directly from the reciprocal Branch-B decoder (zero hard-coded coefficients) and certifying all 21 pair square roots sqrt(1 + x_i*x_j) in Q((h)), proving the ordinary Branch-B full-root cover is everywhere locally soluble over Q_v for every place v; and proved via 2-isogeny descent on E_coll : v^2 = u(u+1)(u+5) (dual torsor W^2 = 2(U^4 - 6U^2V^2 + 4V^4), v_2 in {1, 3}) that rank E_coll(Q) = 0 with all 4 torsion points at poles k in {-3, -1, 1/3, 1} on the anchor-collision conic (u_w - 2u_d)^2 + u_d^2 = 1; (3) Unconditional Kummer 2-Descent & Mod-3, 11, 19 Saturation Certificate on E_B (Theorem 5(3), exp38) and Base-Point Elliptic Sections x+z=3, z=3x-1 (Theorem 7(6), exp38).",
